## Unresolved concerns
- **Retained code (P2, partly open):** hashing is now incremental, but every earlier segment is still kept in memory, even when no live closure refers to it. The reviewer's second point (keep old code only while something can still reach it) needs a way to know which closures are still alive, so I left it.
- **Forged tokens:** round ids stop stale results, not forged ones. Anything else writing to the output stream could stamp a token with our current round id.
- **Empty image:** if an input compiles to an empty stack image, `load-image` now marks the VM halted. Before, the VM would have run on from the end of the held image. No test covers this.
- **`::result-append` on the VM:** it is an extra key on the VM record. It is removed before storage on success, but on the thrown-error path the round's starting VM is restored, so it never persists there either. Cross-host behaviour (CLJS/CLJD) is untested by me, as instructed.
